      "id": "nrj8q5q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.2.2 Atomic Energy"
    },
    {
      "id": "arp7599",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "vvpabx2",
      "src": "/books/Guide/RAJASTHAN SI GS GUIDE/images/image_vvpabx2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Rawatbhata Atomic Power Station (RAPS) is located at Rawatbhata in Chittorgarh district on the banks of Chambal River. It has 6 units and is managed by NPCIL.",
      "id": "mmghdb5"
    },
    {
      "id": "uekg02c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.2.3 Solar Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rajasthan is India's leading state in solar energy generation. It has high solar irradiation (~5-7 kWh/m²/day). The Bhadla Solar Park in Jodhpur is one of the largest solar parks in the world (capacity ~2245 MW). The state also has the Sambhar Salt Lake area proposed for solar projects.",
      "id": "db04030"
    },
    {
      "id": "1liekrf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.2.4 Wind Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rajasthan has significant wind energy potential, especially in Jaisalmer, Barmer, and Jodhpur districts. The Jaisalmer Wind Park is one of the largest in India.",
      "id": "szv3607"
    },
    {
      "id": "396wv7w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.3 Oil & Natural Gas"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Oil and natural gas are found in Barmer-Sanchore basin. ONGC and Cairn India have been involved in extraction. The Mangala oilfield in Barmer is one of the most significant onshore oilfields in India. The Barmer Refinery (HPCL-Rajasthan Refinery Ltd) is under development at Pachpadra.",
      "id": "ryxx3mu"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": false
